### krb5 CVEs

CVE-2022-42898
CVE-2023-39975

### busybox CVEs

CVE-2022-48391
CVE-2023-49604

---

## CATEGORY 2: APPLICATION-LEVEL CVEs (TEMPORARY - SCHEDULED FOR UPGRADE)

These are MEDIUM severity and temporary. Remove immediately after fixes.

Rationale: Low exploitability + local/build-time only + fixed versions ready

### CVE-2026-25645 (requests@2.32.5 - MEDIUM)

Requires: Local attacker with /tmp write access
Context: Backend Python library, production impact low
Fix Available: requests==2.33.0 (patch release, zero breaking changes)

CVE-2026-25645

### CVE-2026-33532 (yaml@2.8.2 - MEDIUM)

Requires: Deep YAML nesting input (>10KB) + attacker control
Context: Build-time only (PostCSS config parser)
Fix Available: yaml@2.8.3 (patch release, zero breaking changes)

CVE-2026-33532

---

## CATEGORY 3: BUILD-TIME NODE DEPENDENCIES (Non-Runtime)

These vulnerabilities are in npm build/dev chains and do NOT affect runtime.

Rationale: Build-time only + Deep deps + Major version upgrades required

### tar (node-tar) - Hardlink/Symlink exploits

GHSA-34x7-hfp2-rc4v
GHSA-8qq5-rm4j-mr97
GHSA-83g3-92jg-28cx
GHSA-qffp-2rhf-9h96
GHSA-9ppj-qmqm-q256
GHSA-r6q2-hw4h-h46w

### @tootallnate/once - Control flow scoping vulnerability

Context: Transitive dependency from http-proxy-agent (build-time)
Impact: Build environment only - not used in runtime code

GHSA-vpq2-c234-7xj6

---

## POLICY & COMPLIANCE NOTES

1. This file is reviewed every 30 days minimum
2. All MEDIUM+ CVEs must have upgrades within SLA 24-48 hours
3. Any CRITICAL CVEs bypass this file entirely - instant remediation required
4. Entries removed immediately upon successful upgrade deployment
5. For audit trail: See git history for when each CVE was resolved
